Jeff Killeen wrote:
> Maybe Todd is finally getting it.  Are you willing to acknowledge that what
> the market values is the amount of computing punch for the dollars expended?
> If your answer is no then why would the market care about your assumption?

In the past, corporations viewed computing in the same way as building a
tower. You know the building will last a long time so you need to have very
strong foundations and a very good design that will keep the tower up no
matter what weather comes, and you will also have to have the means to
renovate floors and perhaps add a few more floors later on. And then once all
of the structure is done and proven solid, you add the decorations.

In the past, the folks knew that initially all the money spent would go
towards less interesting stuff such as structural beams, concrete, digging for
