The DSSI cable doesn't go directly to the system board, it goes to a
small card that plugs into the system board, under the disk drives.

My 4000/100 has the Qbus connector on the top of the case and the back
of the case is flat, like other 3100 systems.  The DSSI cable mounts in
one of the removable covers on the back of the case.

Only one end of the DSSI cable comes out of the case, so the system
needs to be at the end of the DSSI bus.

I can open my system and look for a part numbers on the board and cable
if you want.

Robert



