The problem with Compaq is more than just poor communication, poor
marketing, poor press-releases, poor understanding of the user community
... etc, etc.  The problem is their competence.

There have been too many errors of judgement (eg. extreme emphasis on
the PC side of the business, roadmaps and commitments that are cancelled
before the ink is dry) and their credibility now rates somewhere in the
negatives.

Once customers lose confidence in a supplier they rapidly start to look
elsewhere; those customers who stay with the product, for whatever
reason, become extremely skeptical of any statement from that company
and will examine every statement in microscopic detail.

This is what has happened with Compaq and all too often that detail has
been found to be wanting, thus diminishing their credibility even
further.

Communication is a small part of their problem.  Credibility is the
bigger issue.


