It would be nice if all seller put all the details into the auction,
but they don't all do that.  Though most that have sold many items do.

It is usual to hold a check unless the buyer has a high enough
rating, though how high isn't standard.  I have seen between 10 and
50 as required not to hold a check.

If I want it fast I send a MO, but I usually prefer a check and
usually 14 days is fast enough for me.

I would say that giving someone a negative feedback for waiting for
a check to clear would be enough for him to give you negative feedback.

Many banks charge the depositor $15 or $20 for a bounced check.

