Regarding PDP's and environment problems...

I once had a PDP 11/84 in a computer room with windows to the
outside. During one winter storm, one of the windows was blown
open during the night. An operatior noticed this in the morning
and closed the window. No problems so far with the PDP...

Now, when the window was open, the temp in the computer room
got below 0 deg C (freezing point) and the water based 
heating equipment got frozen (and of course sprung leak, but
since it was froozen nothing happend at that time).

OK, so 15 mins later, when the heater thaw out, the heating
equipment started to leak hot water, and the computer
room turned into a Finish steam sauna. The whole mess was
discovered when the water started pouring down the stair-well...

When I got into the computer room, I could hardly see anything
through all the steam. The hot water (aprox 60 deg C) sprinkled
the roof and dripped down all over the PDP rack and the RL02 drives.

In fact, the users didn't know anything until I hitted the emergency
stop button and broke the power to the computer room...

