> It isn't worth arguing with Bill.

Au contraire.

It's worth it when I'm wrong, because I'll cheerfully (or occasionally
sheepishly) admit it as soon as you've succeeded in explaining why.  And
it's worth it when I'm right as long as you're willing to learn.

The only times it's not worth it are when you're both wrong and ineducable.

