> isn't interesting, but multi-stream is.

While single-stream performance isn't exactly something that can be
'solved', it can certainly be 'improved' - and EV8's extension from 4-way to
8-way issue did exactly that (I think there were a couple of other
applicable tweaks as well).  The fact that its performance impact in
multi-threaded environments was more dramatic doesn't detract from that.

(There's also some interesting research going on into decomposing
single-threaded code into multiple independent - or speculative -
micro-threads that can be scheduled concurrently on an SMT platform.  But
I'm not sufficiently familiar with it to suggest that EV8 could have
achieved even better single-thread performance in this way.)

>
