"B.Eckstein" wrote:
> Do you remember the exact commands ?
> It would be nice to connect my 3190 over DSSI
> to my 4500 and 4600.

When (if!) I track them down, I'll post them.

I don't have a MicroVAX 3100-90 handy
otherwise I could probably work it
out by trial and error.

At the console, type:
>>> T 9E

This gives you a list of tests
that can be used. It does not tell you
how to use them and it does not list
anything that looks like it might be
the conversion you want.

9D looks like a possible candidate, try that one.

When you do find the right test, the required
parameter is the model you wish to switch to.
So if you are a KA50 (uVAX 3100-90) and wish to
become a KA52 (VAX 4000-100) you feed in 52.

It sits there for a while, re-writing its
flash to do this. Don't switch off !!!

I'll go search my email properly tomorrow
to see if I can dig out the exact instructions.
Don't hold your breath!

Antonio

