Intel is already suggesting will be about 1.6 times the performance of
Merced (i.e., pretty much the same improvement one would expect from other
architectures given the year between their introductions, and thus not
noticeably improving Itanic's relative position in the speed sweeps).  Intel
has also indicated that Madison (two generations out from now) will be
McKinley with a process-shrink and more cache, which also promises only to
