It isn't worth arguing with Bill.  If you suggest SMT wasn't solving single
stream performance in EV8, he'll tell you that single stream performance
isn't interesting, but multi-stream is.

The truth is that there is a small segment of users that will pay nearly
anything for the fastest raw performance.  Often their workload cannot be
helped by multiple processors/threads.  For them, IA64 in the short term,
will not be able to compete with Alpha.  There are also users where MP
performance tops out at a specific CPU count, and the only thing that will
help them isn't more CPUs, but faster CPUs... again, short term, IA64 is not
a substitute for Alpha.  For them - EV7&EV79/Marvel will get them the
performance and scaling.

But a great deal of people will be very happy with IA64 performance.  It
will get significantly better over time.  And yes, throwing additional
IA64's at the problem will equal the performance they "might" have gotten on
Alpha.



