They think we are just stuck in a rut and defending what we have out
of habit. They are not aware that VMS is genuinely a better OS than
Unix or Windows nor are they aware that VMS is just as happy on the
desktop as in the datacentre. Therefore they conclude they are doing
us a favour in the long run by weaning us away from VMS. This is the
false perception we must change.

>keep this in the context of prior to the HP merger - I fully agree with you
