No way whatsoever was/is the wet dream of Rosen/Capellas/Winkler to
push Unix. Have you never listened to any of Winkler's speeches to
analysts when he thought we weren't listening?  It;'s all Wintel.
Winkler actually said "We will use Windows to drive into the
soft-under belly of Unix. First we will drive it off the desktop then
into the datacentre until finally we drive Unix out of all but the
most demanding supercomputer applications where it might just hang on
for a while." What part of that is not clear to you?

