news:5ar60u4cjpa63oa1iq044s98bdlu5bn0v4@4ax.com...
> Nothing in Doug Williams presentation on the Alpha-IPF switch
> suggested that the Alpha could not continue to outpace the IA64 for at
> least the next three years. In fact, when pressed, Doug admitted that
> they could probably keep Alpha ahead of the game (but not by much he
> said) for between five and ten years had they executed the EV8 plan.

The issue isn't whether Alpha would have stayed ahead.  The issue is would
have Alpha stayed ahead by enough so that the business reward equaled both
the business risk and the business investment that went along with
continuing Alpha.

Something people forget is one of the reasons, if not the primary reason,
why Ken Olsen was ousted from Digital was because he had serious
reservations whether Alpha would ever generate enough of return to justify
the investment and the risk.  He is on public record about this since he
left the company.  This issue is likely one of the key reasons why GQ Bob
was able to oust him.  The point being is this issue about the risk and
reward of Alpha is a long standing one that goes all the way back to its
Birth...





