Jeff,

alt.sys.pc-clone.compaq is more likely to have someone who can respond very
accurately to your posting.  In the meantime, trot over to www.compaq.com and
search for a BIOS download for your EXACT model of computer.

Compaq often set up a non-DOS diagnostic partition on its hard drives, and the
diagnostic partition contains some of the critical BIOS update software. 

Also, HOLD down F10 as soon as you power up, and keep holding it down.  The
computer will beep and squawk at you, but will show a 301 keyboard error (a la
IBM) and may well offer you the option to enter the BIOS... Ben Myers

