Alice,

First, if the Seagate disk drive is IDE (probable, given it's probable size),
enter the BIOS CMOS setup and enable both IDE channels and autodetect all four
drives: primary, secondary, master, slave.

Second, if the drive is SCSI, most SCSI host adapters detect SCSI devices
attached to them.  DEC used Adaptec 2940-series SCSI adapters, well-behaved and
good quality devices.

Next, make sure your cables are connected securely and correctly oriented.
Also, check drive jumpers either master/slave for IDE or SCSI ID for SCSI.

... Ben Myers

