Robert DiRosario <rdirosario@starpower.net> wrote in
news:3C017FBD.C616B51A@starpower.net: 

>> What do you want to know?
> Mostly just looking for additional information.
> 
> I had my 4000/100 open last week and noticed some jumpers on the DSSI
> card.  I assume those set the ID of the DSSI controller.

DSSI id is set by software - console command is
    	>>>SET DSSI
Try    >>>SET HELP
for more information.

Getting back to your original question.  The "DSSI VAXcluster Installation 
and Troubleshooting Manual" is fairly general and has little to tell you 
about specific hardware other than the KFQSA.  Indeed, my copy EK-410AA-MG-
001 (April 1992) does not mention VAX 4000/100's at all (for a good reason).
    	Chapter 1 DSSI VAxcluster Basics: Hardware & Software
    	Chapter 2 Configuration Rules and Recommendations
    	Chapter 3 Installation
    	Chapter 4 Troubleshooting Tips.
    	Appendix A: Electrical Lengths of Components
    	App B: Calculating Cable Lengths
    	App C: VMS Naming conventions...
    	App D: Accessing a KFQSA without previous ...
    	App E: Sample Configurations with Cables Connected

While I have referred to this manual occasionally, the processor manual is 
generally more informative.

