CR <cr@null.net> wrote:
: Hi,
: I just got a used MV3300. It runs fine.

: Only trouble is the TK70. I feeded a tape and the tape drive is constantly 
: blinking rapidly. Pressing unload brings the orange light to blink slowly 
: for some time, until all lights start blinking frequently again.

: What's up? Broken?

: Many thanks for your help.

Most likely a broken take up leader, or it came off its little hook.

Remove the tape, if you can, and look inside.  There should be a little piece
of what appears to be tape with a mushroom head on it.  It should be caught on
a little spring loaded hook.  If you don't see it, then the take up leader is
broken or has come off of the hook.  It's fairly simple to replace or put it
back on, but if usually requires taking the drive out of the system.

Once the drive is removed from the system, locate the leader, thread it by the
head and all the rollers until it comes out into the cartridge area.  Lay the
little rectangular hole over the hook (you'll probably have to push the hook
arm back - it's spring loaded), and you're done.  Work the leader back and
forth a few times while watching the tape path, to ensure that the leader
isn't caught on anything, and you should be all set.

        Stu


