> I never heard that EV8 didn't work (in fact, the only thing that could or
> could not work would be a simulation as they sure as hell don't have
> bootable silicon) but I've heard from several senior technical types that
> EV8 posed some significant issues, SMT being among them.

You *really* have to be careful when parsing Compaq statements.  For
example, few in the industry would question the fact that applying SMT to an
architecture of any complexity would pose significant issues (just imagine
the difficulty Itanic is going to have in this area) - but the real issue is
whether these issues, which have been being closely examined for years now,
were on-track with respect to being solved for EV8.

