curious to see what this same Mr Fenwick was saying about IA64 last year. I
wouldn't be surprised to have heard him blast IA64 as an inferior architecture
that would have a lot of difficulty catching up to Alpha. 

A year or two ago, I saw a presentation from John Loether who praised Alpha
and blasted the then vapourware IA64 and gave plenty of argumenst against
IA64. I had also seen presentation by other (Digital) employees at the time of
the merger with Compaq indicating that the baggage of IA64 would not allow
Intel to keep up with Alpha because of its bloat and would result in lower
yields, raising the cost of the IA64.

In early september, I saw a presentation from Mr Loether again, and I couldn't
wait to see how he would spin the alpha disaster. He still had his integrity
and managed to skirt the IA64 disaster and did not tout that IA64 would be the
next best thing since sliced bread. He is probably thinking of retiring so he
has nothing to lose by being honest.

Someone mentioned the "get over it" comment from a compaq employee.  This
applies to compaq employees even more than to customers: if they don't toe the
party line, when the time comes to reduce the headcount due to the HP buying
Compaq, guess who will lose their jobs first ? As customers we must understand
the difficult position Compaq employees are in. But that position also means
that we understand that these guys may be forced to say many things that they
do not believe.


