Since your disk is SCSI, the IDE settings wouldn't affect it.  They would
affect the CD-ROM drive, though.  You could disable the primary IDE
interface but leave the secondary enabled, since the CD-ROM drive probably
connects to the secondary.

The SCSI adapter must have BIOS enabled on it, in order to boot from a SCSI
drive.  Find out what kind of SCSI controller is in it and search for
information about how to configure it to enable BIOS.

