First I must say, outstanding stuff and thanks. Second, I have taken alot of
heat about this and stand corrected the OS involved here is RSX-11M not
Unix. I was led to believe that RSX was an early version of Unix but what do
I know? The department of disinformation was obviously hard at work. I have
lots of great info to digest and will do so over the next couple of weeks.
My location is Toronto for those who would like to know. The equipment
involved here is a PDP-1123, M8186, with an M8059KF memory board, an M8043
serial board, a Peritek VRG-Q video board, a DTC host adaptor with a DTC 520
disk controller with a Seagate ST-506 operating system hard disk and a
second one as the data/files drive. There is also a 5 1/4" floppy drive. The
trick with this set up is that the serial card talks with a custom interface
card which in turns talks with the terminal, music keyboard and external
serial ports.




