C-Kermit 8.0 is almost ready for release.  The final Beta (Beta.04),
was announced on the Kermit newsgroup (comp.protocols.kermit.misc)
yesterday:

  http://www.columbia.edu/kermit/ck80b04.html  <-- Beta announcement
  http://www.columbia.edu/kermit/ck80b.html    <-- C-Kermit 8.0 page
  http://www.columbia.edu/kermit/ckermit.html  <-- C-Kermit main page

If you haven't been following C-Kermit 8.0 (or C-Kermit at all), note
that the new release incorporates:

 . Kerberos, SSL/SLS, and SRP security.
 . An SSH interface.
 . Advanced, secure, scriptable Telnet, FTP, and HTTP clients.
 . Lots more; see the web links for details.

So far, Beta.04 (or earlier Betas) has been built successfully on the
following DEC (hardware and/or software) platforms (the ones maked with
"*" need updating):

 Architecture    Operating System    Filename
  Alpha           Tru64 UNIX 4.0E     cku200b04.tru64-40e                
  Alpha           Tru64 UNIX 4.0F     cku200b04.tru64-40f                
 *Alpha           Tru64 UNIX 5.0A     cku200b03.tru64-50a                
  Alpha           Red Hat Linux 6.2   cku200b04.linux-alpha-rh62 
 *MIPS            Ultrix 4.4	      cku200b03.ultrix44-mips            
 *VAX             Ultrix 3.0	      cku199b01.ultrix30-vax             
  VAX             Ultrix 4.5	      cku200b04.ultrix45-vax             
 *VAX             4.3BSD              cku199a02.bsd43c-vax               

Plus many others on VMS, announced separately on comp.os.vms.

If you can build other combinations, please upload the binaries to:

  ftp://kermit.columbia.edu/kermit/incoming/

using the naming conventions illustrated above.  Of particular interest are:

 . OSF/1 all versions
 . Digital UNIX (pre-Tru64) all versions, especially 3.2
 . Other Ultrixes

There's little hope for Ultrix-11 but we'll see.  At least now it has
G-Kermit:

  http://www.columbia.edu/kermit/gkermit.html

If anybody out there has UNIX V6 or V7 on PDP-11, maybe we could get a
G-Kermit for that too.  Or for that matter, Venix or 2.9BSD on Pro-3xx.

I hope the final release will come within a few weeks.  Meanwhile, report
any problems with Beta.04 to:

  kermit-support@columbia.edu

Thanks!

Frank da Cruz
The Kermit Project
Columbia University
New York City
