Dave

While installing NT4.0, a message appears along the lines of

"NT4 setup doesn't recognise the type of computer ... please select from
this list ... or insert a hardware support disk from your manufacturer."

At that stage "Compaq XP1000" doesn't feature on the list.  However, I do
have an NT4 hardware support disk for the machine.  Whan I use it, a new
list appears which includes "Compaq XP1000", which I select and proceed with
the installation.  The disk contains the files

Readme.txt  OEMSETUP.INF  TXTSETUP.OEM  HALTSUUP.DLL  HALTSUMP.DLL
A221264.PAL  ATAPI.SYS  DECKZPSX.SYS

During the failed W2K install, no similar message appears inviting you to
choose a machine type.  The installation just carries on and fails.

Interestingly, in both the NT4 and W2K installations, a route is available
to allow additional storage device drivers to be supplied: 'S' for NT4 (I
think) and 'F6' for W2K.  However this route is definitely not needed to
successfully install NT4.  Looking in TXTSETUP.OEM, it looks like specifying
the machine type "Compaq XP1000" during NT4 installation selects drivers to
be used, specifically ATAPI.SYS.

I suspect I require the ATAPI.SYS driver for W2K.  Does it exist?  Probably
not.

Cheers
Andy

