government is fashioned in a certain manner and has certain powers.  It
says that the remaining powers are the proerty of the people and the
states.  It never says that the rights end at the border, or that
visitors or outsiders shall not also have some rights.  All levels of 
government in the US have recognized that visitors shall have rights.
When visitors, or citizens, are outside the borders they may travel or
reside in areas who's governments don't recognize those rights, but
that's not a fault of the US Constitution.

