Doesn't help. Any competent amateur astronomer, with expenditure of a few
hundred dollars - and there are tens of thousands all over the world - can
find them and compute their orbits with freely available software. The optical
ones are large because of their optical system, the radar ones because they
are power-hungry, and the SIGINT ones because of their large antennas. And the
more difficult they are to find, the less use they are (hint: higher orbits
give less resolution and higher revisit intervals).

