Hello folks:

Good news!  I am working on my TS10 emulator (VAX emulator).  I finally 
get more further than before after I put credits in MSCP packet (Set 
Controller Characteristics Command).  I struggled to get OpenVMS and 
NetBSD to continue for many weeks.  I learned that OpenVMS and NetBSD 
requires least 2 credits before can issue "Get Unit Status" packets to 
continue.

In "Set Controller Characteristics" end message, I put 4 credits or so
into Type field of message header.  VMS and NetBSD finally get more
further... 

NetBSD successfully attached ra0 as RRD40.  It said that device type RRD40 
clearly.  It successfully processed "Get Unit Status" with unit #0 but 
crashed with results from RQDX3 for unit #1.

However, OpenVMS v7.2 did not issue "Get Unit Status" for unit #0 but
starting with unit #1.

I am trying figure out about unit schemes.  I have some questions with
you.  Unit #0 is controller, Unit #1 is drive #0, etc..  Right?  If
not, does anyone have any information about unit schemes?

Does anyone have information about credits handling because both are
sensetive to credits from RQDX3 controller?  They can't go ahead to
issue "Get Unit Status" without least 2 credits from RQDX3 controller.

Yes, I now was able to boot NetBSD/vax from CD directly because CD disc
does not have FILES-11 but ISO-9660 format.  Interesting results in
debug.log about ISO-9660 format.  Each block is 2048 bytes that I noticed.
VMB recongizes both FILES-11 and ISO-9660 format.

Thank you!

-- Tim Stark

