Alpha marketing malfeasance rendered the IPF consolidation the best course
of action Compaq could take. It's way too late to undo the damage that the
original Alpha marketing team did in the early-mid 90's. It's too late to
undo the really lousy deal that Microsoft suckered Strecker into accepting
in August 1995 (Alliance for Enterprise Computing). And it's too late to
undo the cancellation of the Sculptor project by the dynamic duo of
Eckhard and Enrico.

