review of the record will show:
Intel paid Digital a sum of coin of the realm.
Intel acquired the fab facility.
Intel acquired the legal right to produce the things being produced
in the fab.
Intel became unencumbered as to the use of DEC proprietary
technologies that Intel had already incorporated into its product
line, perhaps without proper legal agreements to allow them to do 
just that.
Thus Alan's concise and accurate conclusion: Intel bought DEC.
A more precise definition might be possible, but it would be
no where near as succient.
