Robert DiRosario wrote:
> 
> I'm working on configuring a B400x expansion box for my VAX 4000/106A.
> I don't have VMS installed yet, so I'm using the console "configure"
> command.
> The system will not recognize "KLESI".  What do I need to enter for this
> card?
> 
> The board order that I selected,  from right to left is:
> 
> TQK70
> KLESI
> DPV11
> DESQA
> DESQA
> CXA16
> CXY08
> KDA50
> 
> I've never configured a Qbus system before.  Will the board
> order I selected work?
> 
> The box had a M9060-YAA1 board in it.  Is that just a load board?  With
> the above
> cards, two RF7x drives, two RF3x drives and a TK70 drive do I need the
> load board?
> I don't see a minium power load listed in the SOC.
> 
> Thanks
> Robert

The KLESI is an MSCP interface. It is used with both disk (RC-25) and
tape (TU-8x) devices. If your device is a tape drive use TK70. If a disk
use KDA50.

The CONFIGURE command will give you a list of Qbus addresses and vectors
for each of the cards. You must set all of your modules to the list's
values for addresses and vectors.

The module's address is set (programmed) by DIP switch packs, or
jumpered pin blocks (or sometimes by wire wrapped pins). The module's
address must be changed to the address shown by the CONFIGURE command.

Likewise with each module's vector address. Some modules, like the DESQA,
have a software programmable vector and thus do not have a hardware
setable vector.


