> advantage yet?
>

Yep. David Fenwick.

> Alpha is gone. Even with all the money etc, the time lost is fatal.
> Now watch T64 and VMS go the same way.
>

I wouldn't be investing much stock in Tru64 futures, but VMS will likely
be in a stronger position once the IPF port is complete (at least one
cross-compiler is up and running now).

But it all comes back to marketing. Instead of shooting the messenger, why
not focus on the source of the problem?



