Kevin Handy wrote:
> Is there a way of generating this ROM file having a working MicroVaxII?
> There should be some way to dump the rom contents from the  '>>>'
> prompt and then generating a fle from that. Anyone have the
> correct procedures?

The easy way is to take the EPROM, drop it
in a programmer and have it dump the contents.

From the console you could try
>>> E/P/N:? 20040000

where ? is the size of the chunk you are
dumping.

Except that I just checked and it looks
like the MicroVAX II console does not
know about the /N qualifier.

OTOH the DEPOSIT command *does* know about
/N so maybe the manual just forgot
to mention that it works with EXAMINE?

Failing that you can try the BINARY UNLOAD
command:
>>> X 20040000 count <RETURN>

you need to set bit 31 of the count
otherwise it is a BINARY LOAD command!
Allegedly designed for use by
automated systems - I've never tried it
myself!

If you have your favourite OS running,
just map the EPROM and dump as you
prefer (I did this years ago using
OpenVMS on a MicroVAX 3900 before
I had access to an EPROM burner).


Antonio

