Kaz,

1. Check the master-slave jumper setting on the hard drives.
2. Clear the CMOS and then see if the drive autodetects.
3. The Venturis FX has an older and quirky Phoenix BIOS limited to just under
8.4GB in capacity.  If you're trying to use a larger drive, you'll need an
add-on card with built-in hard disk BIOS.  An older ISA bus card will do, and
you'll have to be careful to get an older PCI card, because the PCI in the FX
complies with version 2.0.  Newer PCI 2.1 cards don't always work.

... Ben Myers

