I think this is a clock vs. performance issue.  If you have a choice
between developing an SMT processor that can run 4 threads at 1.4 GHz
or a single-thread processor at 2.4 GHz (made up the numbers, but I
don't think they are ridiculous), which will give better real-world
performance?  Maybe you're better off with the much slower SMT
processor, or maybe you're better off with the other.  Unless the 1GHz
difference completely destroys any advantage of SMT, I don't see
why this would justify abandoning Alpha.  Of course, you no longer
have meaningless clock-speed bragging rights.  So even if true, this
statement helps clarify things very much.  We need more information.

