Paul Repacholi wrote:
> 
> Robert DiRosario <rdirosario@starpower.net> writes:
> 
> > I want to install a KDA50 in a B400x box.  (And one in a B213 box.)
> 
> > Is there any difference between the board set for BA23/BA123 (Q/22)
> > systems and B2xx/B4xx (Q/CD) systems?
> 
> Yes. There are a pair of 0 ohm jumpers on each board. These
> should be removed for a stricktly comforming CD bus slot. In
> practice it don't matter a damm... normally

True.

The jumpers are needed in a BA23/BA123
(i.e. a Q-Q slot) to pass the grants
along so that boards further down the chain
will work (ignoring, for now, the fact that
most boards prefer to be nearer the CPU than
the KDA50).

In a Q-CD slot, depending on what the next board down is,
you may not wish to pass along the signals (since
they might upset that board).

But in reality, unless there is a board
in the next slot further down, and it is
a quad board rather than a dual height
board *and* it cares about those signals,
then you should be fine.

Antonio

