Hello folks:

I struggle to get my RQDX3 emulator working with real OpenVMS operating
system.  I sucessfully loaded and run OpenVMS because VMB and SYSBOOT
just uses three simple MSCP commands - Set Controller Char. Command, 
Online Command, and Read Command.  It uses poll register to process
commands to complete.  VMB successfully loaded and ran SYSBOOT.
SYSBOOT successfully loaded some image files and started OpenVMS
execution by enter EXE$INIT routine.  OpenVMS loaded some additional
image files like process management, security, etc. - Successful but...

OpenVMS successfully completed the RQDX3 initialization with using
interrupts.  Each step, RQDX3 did send an interrupt to VAX to wake
up OpenVMS to process next step.  I ended up some problems with
step 4 initialization.  OpenVMS wants a last fail message packet
by set LF bit in step 4 initialization.  My MQDX manual said that
a last fail message packet is sent when controller error occurs or
a LF bit set in step 4 initialization.  That's mean OpenVMS still
am waiting for a last fail message to complete initialization.
I tried that.  OpenVMS received a last fail message but tossed it away
without process any in that.  Then OpenVMS went into sleep for some time
before it started to send first MSCP command - Set Controller
Char. Command.  It received results from my RQDX3 emulator
and processed it successfully.  However, it did not issue ONLINE or GET
UNIT STATUS, etc commands to get unit information.  Instead it
went back to sleep until timeout occured.

Due to lack of MSCP specifications, it is much difficult to develop
the RQDX3 emulator for my VAX emulator.  Also, I do not have diagnostics
to test RQDX3 emulator like HCORE/KLAD tests. :-(  Does anyone have
diagnostics for VAX to test MSCP devices, etc?

Debug Log Step Summary
----------------------

Prints "OpenVMS (tm) ...." welcome message.

Start re-initialization on RQDX3 emulator by write 0 to IP.
Received 054000 from SA (Step #1)
Send 122377 to SA. (Step #1)
   Response - 16 slots, Commands - 16 slots, Vector = 774. IE bit set.

Received an interrupt from RQDX3
Received 010244 from SA (Step #2)
Send 142120 to SA (Step #2)
   PI - No, Low Ringbase - C450

Received an interrupt from RQDX3
Received 020377 from SA (Step #3)
   Vector = 774.
Send 000003 to SA
  PP - No. High Ringbase - 0003
  (Ringbase Address is 3C450)

Received an interrupt from RQDX3
Received 040463 from SA (Step #4)
Send 020003 to SA
  GO, LF, and Burst 0 set up but '2' - Unknown

Received an interrupt from RQDX3
Received 000000 from SA. (Ready)

Process '040463' as model 19, rev 3.
Labels RQDX3 as 'SABKUP$PUA:'.
Check any response results from RQDX3 - No messages.
Went to sleep for a while...

Send SCCC command to RQDX3
Received results of SCCC command from RQDX3.
Received an interrupt.
Check both descriptors and found two packets (one - command and one - 
   response) were completed.
Processed results but do nothing for additional commands, etc.
Went to sleep until timeout occured.
  Timeout set off, cause re-initialization back to step #1. :-(

Thank you!

-- Tim Stark

