Tim,

The LF bits means send a last fail packet if one is available,
otherwise, you don't have to.  Since VMS will basically toss them in
the error log, you never really have to send one.  If you do send one,
it's a very different kettle of fish:

Circuit ID = diagnostic (0xFF)
Message type = datagram
Credits = n/a (might as well be 0)

I don't know what VMS may be waiting for.  If the disks are powered up
and spinning at boot time, there shouldn't be any UNIT NOW AVAILABLE
attention messages generated, which only occur if a unit transitions
from offline to available while the controller is up and running.

/Bob

