Hello,
 
My name is Peter, and I am working on the Helicopter Flight Simulator
using the Ersatz PDP-11/45 emulator.  The emulator has been running
successufully and the build of the helicopter Flight Simulator (FS) is
carried out on the emulator and the binary is transferred to the live
PDP and it runs perfectly.
 
I have developed a utility program for capturing data from the
helicopter simulator which is running perfectly on the emulator but
when I transfer it to the real PDP-11 it has problems and I was
wondering if some one could give some suggestion what is happening.
The utility program I had built seemed to be producing garbage so I
wrote the program called NUMGEN.MAC which is at the end of this email.
 It was to check the validity of my input data and output data.
 
The program NUMGEN.MAC generates numbers from 1 ..5120 (20*256).  It
fills a buffer of 256 words (2 bytes each) each time and writes the
buffer to disk. It puts one number in each word. The program outputs
numbers begining from 1 through TO 256. So the first buffer will be
from 1..256, the next buffer 257 .. 512 and so forth. When the program
has written 20 buffers it exits.  The program writes the data to a
binary file called NUMDAT.001 which I have not inclulded because it is
binary, but I can emsil a copy if requested, or you can create it by
extracting the NUMGEN program below and run it on the PDP.
 
The binary file NUMDAT.001 is converted from binary integers to ascii
numbers using the C program FSBD2A.CP (flight simulator binary data to
ascii).  This program outputs a line of five columns.  The first four
columns are the data from NUMDAT.001 converted and the last column on
the right is the running total of all the records that have been read.
 
Segments from the file EMUDAT.TXT are included and it is the data
produced from the PDP emulator and this is correct and this is what I
am expecting as the correct output from the emulator and the PDP.
 
The output from the PDP is not altogether garbage.  There is some
interesting consistency in the output from the PDPDAT.001.  The first
six records are correct.  Then the seventh record is 256 + 7 = 263. 
Then this runs through adding one correctly right up to the 256 record
which is 512.  512 = 256 + 256.  Then it corrects itself again and for
the next six records writes the correct data 256, 257, ... 262. Then
amazingly it then writes 519, 520, 521 and continues correctly after
missing the fist six numbers which were correct.  The pattern is after
outputing the first six numbers correctly it will add 256 to the
remaining 250 numbers.  Then after the 256th number is output
correctly it then writes the next six numbers in the correct sequence
and after the seventh add 256.
 
I know the problem is happening at the real PDP because as soon as the
program was run I run the dump facility on the output file numdat.001
and it was already corrupted.  So I know that it is not my C program
converting the data from binary to ascii which is causing this
problem. At first this is what I had suspected.
 
If there is any help or pointers that you can suggest would be greatly
appreciated.

Note the following, the helicopter simulator when generated on the
emulator and transferred to the PDP-11 works perfectly and has been
for years. So it would be reasonable to assume the simple program
shown below which works on the emulator should work on the PDP.
 
 
