Robert DiRosario wrote:
> 
> I would like to add some RA drives to one of my VAXes at home.
> The RA7x drives are nice and small.  Do they have the 4 pin or 5 pin
> power connector?

Four pin IIRC.

> I have a MicroVAX 3800 is a BA213 chassis that has DSSI drives, and the
> 5 pin power cables.  I would like to put the drives in there.
> What is the part number for the internal RA cables?

RA drives are not DSSI drives so you'll need
a KDA50 rather than your KFQSA (you may already
know this, but just in case!).

I don't recall the part num for the
internal SDI cables. If there are any left
in the office, I'll find the number.

> I see RA9x drives out on the web.  Does each RA9x drive have it's own
> box with a power supply and use the the BC26V cables?

RA9x drives typically come in a larger enclosure
(e.g. a DECarray cab) and these are usually
pre-wired. You just need the same SDI cables
as you would for any other RAx drive.

RA9x drives are pretty heavy - much, much heavier
than an RA7x.

Antonio

