In alt.sys.pdp10 Jeff Campbell <jcampbell@ins-msi.com> wrote:
> Does your emulator (vax/rqdx3) implement the port hardware interrupt
> service routine? The IPL 8 is a software fork level interrupt. I do not
> know if the VMS PUDRIVER interrupt processing handles the communication
> rings transitions. My guess is that it does.

Jeff,

My emulator does implement the port hardware interrupt service routines.
RQDX3/Q22 sent IPL 16 to VAX to interrupt OpenVMS after command
descriptor was executed or each step value for initialization was 
received.  DSR Interrupt will not happen until MTFR changed to IPL 8
from 1F or 18.

> I assume your emulator code is trapping references to rqdx3 polling
> register (IP). If the command ring is not empty when a new command
> packet
> is inserted into the command ring the driver may not poll, giving your
> symptom of hanging/time-out reinit.

Yes, that's why...

My debug log file showed only one command descriptor that contains STCON 
command and other descriptors are zero.

Hmmm.  If STCON command has timeout 120 so that RXQD3 runs out of time 
that waiting for another poll or so then re-issue interrupt?  Or each
timeout of 120, RQDX3 checked command descriptor or so?  For timeout 120, 
it uses microseconds or milliseconds?

Also, I have not seen any commands but only STCON command was posted
by OpenVMS before it polls.

Thank you.

-- Tim Stark

P.S. STCON = Set Controller Characteristics Command

