That would be my first suggestion.  If it runs fine from the BIOS and
yet fails from within NT 4.0, my first guess might be a driver issue. 

One other thing that you might check is the Disk Caching scheme.  You
have a choice of either Write Through or Write Back.  Now, I'm having
a severe case of the stupids right now (and I'm dead tired), but one
of these writes the data to disk immediately and the other one caches
the information to be written and then writes it as it gets an
opportunity.  I can't remember which is which right now, but I believe
that Write Back is the NON-Cached option.  If that works and yet Write
Through does NOT, then you might have a bad cache chip on the board.


