And more foibles with Netscape for the actual patch download:
(no external ftp access, so Netscape it has to be)

My first attempt using Netscape Gold on Alpha VMS (V7.2-1H+) resulted in a
file which didn't match the checksum. The file size matched OK.

Downloading using Netscape on NT and doing a binary FTP across to VMS resulted in
a file which _did_ produce a checksum match, albeit with naming difficulties en
route. *

Investigation showed that the version produced by Netscape on VMS had arrived
as "Stream_LF, maximum 32767 bytes. longest 32767 bytes", the one via the NT route
as "Fixed length 512 byte records".

The solution:

$ SET FILE /ATTRIB=(RFM:FIX,LRL:512) kitname

and the file now gives the correct checksum.

* Netscape 4.n on NT insists on replacing the .PCSI-DCX_AXPEXE extension with
.PCSI. Manually entering the correct extension in the dialog box results in
an extension of .PCSI-DCX_AXPEXE.PCSI.

A useful addition to the FAQ? It would be nice to see this in the standard
paragraphs about the self-extracting format in the cover letter / readme
as well, although realize that could be a lot of work.

