sword7@speakeasy.org writes:
> Also, I discovered that OpenVMS is complete interrupt-driven operating
> system with multi-tier IPL levels.  OpenVMS uses IPL 8 to process
> device interrupt services from multi-level Q22 interrupts (200 to
> 3F4).  According to my book, I learned that there are groups of
> vectors can be specifically to IPL interrupt.  For example, 3C0 to 3F4
> is IPL BR7 (17), etc..  Does anyone have any suggestions?

From a hardware point of view, the vector and IPL are completely orthogonal.
In a given hardware configuration, a particular device will generally always
be assigned the same vector, but the IPL may be set to any level.  Some
devices require the vector to be configured by jumpers, but others including
the RQDX3 are software configurable.

I don't have any idea about the VMS conventions for vectors or IPLs, though.
I'm only familiar with how this is done on PDP-11s.  The Qbus hardware
requirements are the same as for Qbus VAXen, but the vectors are probably
different.


